--[[
	Anomaly Coop - what a theme of the co-op window has to say, and what stands in for it (coop_menu_theme_base.script)

	The window's logic (coop_menu.script) holds no colour, font, art rule, duration or layout number. They are in a theme: a plain
	table `theme` in coop_menu_theme.script. gamedata\ holds the one of plain Anomaly; the same path in a pack's layer replaces
	it (gamedata_gamma\scripts\coop_menu_theme.script for G.A.M.M.A., the layer "Anomaly Coop - GAMMA" right above Core). This
	file is never replaced: DEFAULTS is the complete table, so a theme names only what it changes, and a field that is missing or
	broken takes the default instead of a crash. A new pack needs a theme in its own layer and no change in the code.

	load() -> the resolved theme of this game, a fresh table each time (the window may keep it).

	Colours are { r, g, b [, alpha 0..1] }; a role is a key of `colors`. Fonts: `fonts.register` is what the window hands to
	RegisterFont(name, texture_base[, shader]); `fonts.roles` is role -> { name = for GetFontByName, stock = a stock font when
	the exe has no such font }. Text styles: `text`, name -> { font = role, color = role }. Numbers of `layout` are pixels of a
	1920 x 1080 design, durations are milliseconds, curves are the four numbers of a cubic-bezier.
--]]

local type, pairs, ipairs, pcall, tostring = type, pairs, ipairs, pcall, tostring

DEFAULTS = {
	-- false: nothing moves, every state is reached at once
	motion = true,

	design = { w = 1920, h = 1080 },

